{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the man who acts willfully.</b> This is a sage from among the sages of Israel who wishes to disagree with the Great Court (בית דין) and issues a ruling for himself contrary to the opinion of the Great Court in a matter whose willfulness incurs excision (כרת) and whose inadvertence incurs a sin-offering (חטאת). He is called a rebellious elder (זקן ממרא), and he is liable to the death penalty. <b>And that man shall die.</b> The court shall put him to death."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:59.015148195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}